priya: quick check — staging inference-svc healthchecks started failing after we flipped to NLB TLS passthrough + ALB in front. ALB shows 503s for the backend. healthcheck path is /_healthz and probe type is HTTPS. anyone seen this pattern?

james_k: are we terminating TLS at the ALB or doing passthrough to the pod?

priya: passthrough to pod (NLB) for the inference path, but there's an ALB in front doing SNI-based routing for some tenants. traffic chain: client -> ALB (SNI) -> NLB (TLS passthrough) -> nodeport -> pod. healthcheck currently goes to ALB which then tries HTTPS. not sure how ALB -> NLB healthcheck mapping works here.

samir: ALBs won't do TCP passthrough — their healthchecks are HTTP/HTTPS to the target. If the ALB is probing the NLB endpoint, that can fail since NLB expects TCP/SSL. We usually put the healthcheck on NLB directly or use TCP checks.

maria_g: common pattern: set ALB healthcheck to a lightweight path on the target that can be served without TLS negotiation, or switch ALB healthcheck to TCP if you rely on passthrough. But with TLS passthrough the ALB can't inspect path for SNI routing, so you may need the ALB to use TCP checks or move the healthcheck to the NLB.

priya: here's the terraform snippet we were planning — was going to add aws annotations to the k8s svc: 
```hcl
resource "kubernetes_service" "inference" {
  metadata {
    name = "inference-svc"
    annotations = {
      "service.beta.kubernetes.io/aws-load-balancer-type" = "nlb"
      "service.beta.kubernetes.io/aws-load-balancer-healthcheck-protocol" = "HTTPS"
      "service.beta.kubernetes.io/aws-load-balancer-healthcheck-path" = "/_healthz"
    }
  }
  spec {
    type = "NodePort"
    external_traffic_policy = "Cluster"
    ports { port = 443 target_port = 8080 }
  }
}
```

james_k: two quick notes: (1) target_port should be the container port (8080) that's speaking TLS — fine. (2) external_traffic_policy Cluster makes probelocal IP spin up different behavior; for NLB passthrough + healthchecks we usually set external_traffic_policy = "Local" so the node proxy preserves client src and healthchecks hit the node port correctly.

samir: +1. Also consider switching healthcheck-protocol to TCP for the NLB. If you need application-level healthchecks behind TLS, add an ALB listener that terminates TLS for the health endpoint only (or use a dedicated health endpoint on a separate port without TLS).

priya: hmm curious: we rely on SNI routing on ALB to map tenants, so we can't terminate TLS at ALB globally. Could we add an ALB rule that routes a special hostname (internal-health.<cluster>) to a target group that does HTTPS termination and probes /_healthz unencrypted to the LB? Ugly.

maria_g: you can also run the probe on a plain TCP port on the pod (e.g., 32001) and expose that via a second port in the svc with a different nodePort and have the healthcheck point to that port. Keeps TLS untouched for inference traffic.

priya: that might be the cleanest. add second port block: port 8081 (probe) targetPort 9000 (unsecured) nodePort 32100. Then set lb annotation healthcheck-port = "32100" and protocol = TCP.

james_k: yes — minimal surface change, Terraform change below should work: 
```hcl
ports {
  port = 443
  target_port = 8080
}
ports {
  name = "probe"
  port = 8081
  target_port = 9000
  node_port = 32100
}
metadata {
  annotations = {
    "service.beta.kubernetes.io/aws-load-balancer-healthcheck-protocol" = "TCP"
    "service.beta.kubernetes.io/aws-load-balancer-healthcheck-port" = "32100"
  }
}
spec {
  external_traffic_policy = "Local"
}
```

priya: ok i'll try that in a quick staging patch. any objections to external_traffic_policy = Local on this service? it can affect load distribution.

samir: Local is fine for inference svc since we prefer node-local LB for sticky GPU routing. Just ensure PodDaemonSet and node spread so nodes have backends.

maria_g: also double-check security groups — nodeport probing requires SG open from LB to nodeport. I hit that once where SG blocked the new nodePort.

priya: good call, will add SG rule check to the PR description and run a smoke curl from a bastion after deploy.

deploy-bot: deployment queued for inference/staging (pr/4321) — awaiting CI. (reaction :eyes:)

priya: thanks all — i'll open the terraform + k8s svc PR, run SG check, and ping @james_k for quick review. if CI passes i'll schedule a canary to validate healthchecks and routing. :thumbsup:
